(FICTIONAL SAMPLE DOCUMENT. Halverson Ridge Middle School, Fall 2026, week 5. Written by S.) Tj T*
(Frankel \(Algebra Foundations\) with input from L. Moreau \(Digital Photography\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Algebra. Talia can usually carry out each step of a problem on its own, but she loses track) Tj T*
(of what the question is asking partway through multi-step word problems. On the last quiz) Tj T*
(she set up two equations correctly and then answered a different question from the one on) Tj T*
(the page. She has not turned in three of the last five algebra assignments, and when I) Tj T*
(asked, she said she did not know where to start once she got home.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Attendance. Her absences are clustered on Mondays, and she has missed several of our) Tj T*
(lunchtime review sessions. When she is here she participates, so the gap is time in the room) Tj T*
(rather than effort.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At conferences her mother asked whether Talia might have ADHD, since she finds it hard to) Tj T*
(settle into written work at home. I said that was a question for the counselor and the) Tj T*
(family doctor, not for me.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Photography. Ms. Moreau reports that her photographs show a real eye for composition and) Tj T*
(exposure, and she is often the first to help classmates with their camera settings. Unlike) Tj T*
(Marcus, who rushes his edits, Talia takes her time and asks good questions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Writing. Her short stories in Creative Writing have a clear narrative structure with a) Tj T*
(strong opening, even when her spelling and punctuation slip.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Suggested next step: a short weekly check-in, and some help breaking word problems into) Tj T*
(parts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
